# =============================================================================
# WHAT THIS FILE IS
# Tells Git how to handle line endings and binary files. The project is edited
# on Windows, WSL and Linux, so without these rules files flip between CRLF and
# LF, diffs show every line as changed, and scripts can break in Linux CI.
# =============================================================================

# Normalise line endings so Windows and WSL editors don't produce whole-file diffs.
# Git detects text files and keeps them as LF everywhere, even on Windows checkout.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files: never convert line endings (it would corrupt them) or show text diffs.
*.png binary
*.zip binary
